<article class="env-proposition" id="09QY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09QY">Proposition <span data-tag="09QY">22.27.16</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/09QJ" data-tag="09QJ">22.27.2</a> the homotopy category $K(\mathcal{A})$ with its natural translation functors and distinguished triangles is a triangulated category. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/09QW" data-tag="09QW">22.27.14</a> we know that $K(\mathcal{A})$ is pre-triangulated. Combining Lemmas <a href="/tag/09QN" data-tag="09QN">22.27.7</a> and <a href="/tag/09QX" data-tag="09QX">22.27.15</a> with Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/014C" data-tag="014C">13.4.15</a>, we conclude that $K(\mathcal{A})$ is a triangulated category. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>